# Implementation Plan - Real Data Seeding and Item Model Update

The goal is to update the `Item` model to support a secondary name (`name2`) from the Express database (`STKDES2`) and provide a new management command to seed real items from a gitignored data source.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - The new `name2` field will be added to the `Item` model.
> - A new management command `seed_items_real` will be created.
> - You will need to export your notebook data to `private/data/items.json` for the seeder to work.

## Proposed Changes

### Catalog Model Updates

#### [MODIFY] [item.py](file:///Users/pitsanunamnil/Desktop/work/tj/tj_inventory/django/catalog/models/item.py)
- Add `name2` field (CharField, max_length=200, blank=True).
- Update `save()` method to strip whitespace from `name2`.

### Seeding Logic

#### [NEW] [seed_items_real.py](file:///Users/pitsanunamnil/Desktop/work/tj/tj_inventory/django/catalog/management/commands/seed_items_real.py)
- A new Django management command that reads from `private/data/tj_items.json`.
- It will map:
    - `STKCOD` -> `sku` and `express_sku`
    - `STKDES` -> `name`
    - `STKDES2` -> `name2`
    - `QUCOD` -> `unit`
- It will use `ItemService.create` or `ItemService.update` (if exists) to ensure data integrity.

